Software Engineer 20262859 
 - SALARY INDICATION In consultation - FUNCTION GROUP Engineering - JOB POSTING NUMBER 20262859 - LOCATION Veldhoven Area 
 ABOUT THIS JOB OPENING 
Our client is an innovative organization in the manufacturing industry. To expand its engineering team, we are looking for an enthusiastic Software Engineer with a customer-focused mindset and a passion for industrial automation. 
What will you be doing? 
As a Software Engineer, you will be responsible for developing, testing, and optimizing control software for machines and systems. You will work according to technical specifications and make a significant contribution to new developments and process improvements. 
Your responsibilities: 
• Testing, analyzing, and optimizing machines and systems; 
• Developing and implementing new software solutions; 
• Programming and modifying PLC controls (preferably Siemens S7); 
• Supporting new product and system developments; 
• Collaborating closely with various internal departments; 
• Improving the functionality, reliability, and performance of machines. 
Who are you? 
• HBO-level education and thinking skills, for example in ICT, Electrical Engineering, Industrial Automation, or Mechanical Engineering; 
• 1 to 5 years of relevant work experience in a similar position; 
• Experience with embedded systems and industrial software development; 
• Knowledge of PLC programming, preferably Siemens S7; 
• Willing to travel internationally on an occasional basis; 
• Independent, proactive, and solution-oriented; 
• Flexible and able to handle stress well; 
• Strong communication skills in both Dutch and English; 
• Ability to perform excellently both independently and as part of a team. 
What do we offer? 
• A varied role within an innovative and growing organization; 
• Plenty of room for initiative, professional development, and training; 
• An excellent salary commensurate with your experience; 
• Attractive benefits; 
• ...

Looking for a job with fixed hours and want to work with a big logistics company? Look no further and apply now! You'll be working in a large warehouse in Wijchen, part of an international logistics organisation. From four warehouses on the same site, large volumes of goods go out every day to customers across Europe and beyond. Your work keeps that moving. You operate the EPT and make sure pallets get to the right place. You do that independently and accurately. When things get busy somewhere, you pitch in on another task. Nothing complicated, just doing your job well.

 - Proven, recent hands-on experience operating an EPT;
 - Available in dayshift Monday to Friday, 40 hours per week;
 - You speak and understand Dutch or English.
